1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:02,123
JONAH: Okay. Okay okay okay. OKAY!

2
00:00:02,473 --> 00:00:04,781
Moon. Let's go to the Moon.

3
00:00:06,081 --> 00:00:08,081
[TWO HOURS EARLIER — Lagos, Nigeria · 2:07 AM]

4
00:00:08,581 --> 00:00:13,581
EXECUTOR: Two in the morning. A phone
repair stall the size of a wardrobe.

5
00:00:13,931 --> 00:00:18,825
Jonah Okafor, seventeen. Could fix anything
with a wire in it. Could sleep through

6
00:00:18,825 --> 00:00:20,854
anything, including Lagos traffic.

7
00:00:21,654 --> 00:00:25,500
MRS. BELLO: It was my husband's. It
hasn't spoken since he passed.

8
00:00:25,850 --> 00:00:27,773
JONAH: Give me ten minutes, Ma.

9
00:00:28,573 --> 00:00:33,958
EXECUTOR: He fixed it in nine. She held out
her coins. He wouldn't take them.

10
00:00:34,308 --> 00:00:35,208
Nobody saw.

11
00:00:36,158 --> 00:00:38,431
Nobody, that is... except me.

12
00:00:39,231 --> 00:00:40,131
Item One.

13
00:00:40,781 --> 00:00:44,977
To the one who fixes what
everyone else throws away...

14
00:00:45,727 --> 00:00:47,265
we leave our ship.

15
00:00:48,765 --> 00:00:52,565
[THE BLINK FILES · FILE 01 · THE WILL · Item One: The Ship]

16
00:00:53,065 --> 00:00:58,450
EXECUTOR: Find Orion. Three stars for a
belt. And on his shoulder, a red one.

17
00:00:58,800 --> 00:00:59,700
Betelgeuse.

18
00:01:01,700 --> 00:01:04,008
Six days ago, it went out.

19
00:01:05,158 --> 00:01:12,045
It did not explode. A star that size should
die in a blaze bright enough to see at

20
00:01:12,045 --> 00:01:12,465
noon.

21
00:01:12,815 --> 00:01:16,627
It just... went dark. Like
someone flipped a switch.

22
00:01:17,427 --> 00:01:22,427
Orion can be seen from every country on
Earth. So every country noticed.

23
00:01:24,727 --> 00:01:29,427
Three days later, every radio on Earth
picked up the same broadcast. Every

24
00:01:29,427 --> 00:01:31,650
frequency. Every language. At once.

25
00:01:32,450 --> 00:01:36,296
This is the last will and
testament of the Vey.

26
00:01:37,046 --> 00:01:38,200
We are gone.

27
00:01:39,150 --> 00:01:42,962
We leave everything we
owned... to twelve of you.

28
00:01:44,762 --> 00:01:46,685
Twelve heirs. Eight billion candidates.

29
00:01:47,035 --> 00:01:52,724
Nobody slept. Several million people checked
under their beds. A man in Ohio dug up

30
00:01:52,724 --> 00:01:53,958
his entire garden.

31
00:01:54,758 --> 00:01:59,373
Jonah did what Jonah always did. He
went home and fixed things.

32
00:02:01,673 --> 00:02:02,573
Jonah Okafor?

33
00:02:02,923 --> 00:02:04,042
JONAH: ...Who's there?

34
00:02:04,842 --> 00:02:08,688
EXECUTOR: I am the Executor of
the estate of the Vey.

35
00:02:09,038 --> 00:02:11,346
Congratulations. You are Heir Number One.

36
00:02:12,146 --> 00:02:14,454
He threw a flip-flop at me.

37
00:02:15,104 --> 00:02:18,181
Statistically, that is the most
common human response.

38
00:02:18,981 --> 00:02:20,135
Please. Step outside.

39
00:02:22,835 --> 00:02:28,988
Five metres of hull. Nothing on Earth can
see it, unless it wants to be seen.

40
00:02:30,788 --> 00:02:32,292
JONAH: Is that... mine?

41
00:02:32,642 --> 00:02:33,542
EXECUTOR: Legally? Entirely.

42
00:02:34,342 --> 00:02:36,650
The neighbour's goat was not impressed.

43
00:02:38,450 --> 00:02:43,065
Every inheritance comes with rules.
The Vey were very fond of rules.

44
00:02:43,865 --> 00:02:47,712
Rule One. The ship answers
to you, and only you.

45
00:02:48,062 --> 00:02:51,138
Rule Two. It will never carry a weapon.

46
00:02:51,488 --> 00:02:54,565
Rule Three. It must be
home before sunrise.

47
00:02:55,965 --> 00:03:01,328
A note on translation. The Vey word for
"home" means, literally, "the place where

48
00:03:01,328 --> 00:03:04,042
you sleep." The Vey were not sentimental.

49
00:03:04,842 --> 00:03:09,073
JONAH: And if I'm not in it
when the sun comes up?

50
00:03:09,423 --> 00:03:13,269
EXECUTOR: Then you will be
wherever you are. For a while.

51
00:03:13,619 --> 00:03:16,696
Break any rule, and the
inheritance is void.

52
00:03:17,496 --> 00:03:19,419
JONAH: How do I drive it?

53
00:03:19,769 --> 00:03:22,462
EXECUTOR: You don't drive it. You ask it.

54
00:03:22,812 --> 00:03:23,712
JONAH: ...Up?

55
00:03:24,912 --> 00:03:25,812
EXECUTOR: Up.

56
00:03:29,812 --> 00:03:35,137
At one hundred kilometres, the sky stops being
blue. Officially, that is where space

57
00:03:35,137 --> 00:03:35,581
begins.

58
00:03:37,381 --> 00:03:40,423
JONAH: That's... that's Africa.
That's ALL of Africa.

59
00:03:40,773 --> 00:03:45,773
Grandma is down there. Mrs. Bello is down
there. Everybody is down there.

60
00:03:47,573 --> 00:03:51,035
EXECUTOR: Sunrise in Lagos was
at 6:42. It was 2:51.

61
00:03:51,385 --> 00:03:55,231
He had less than four hours,
and the whole planet.

62
00:03:56,031 --> 00:03:59,877
First, the Sahara. No city lights
for a thousand kilometres.

63
00:04:00,227 --> 00:04:05,996
He lay on a dune where the stars were
so thick the sky looked dusty.

64
00:04:07,596 --> 00:04:09,519
JONAH: Executor. Which one was yours?

65
00:04:10,669 --> 00:04:12,173
EXECUTOR: ...The dark one.

66
00:04:14,373 --> 00:04:20,142
Then he did something nobody had told him
he could do. He chased the night.

67
00:04:20,492 --> 00:04:26,072
The Earth turns east at about sixteen hundred
and seventy kilometres an hour. Fly

68
00:04:26,072 --> 00:04:29,723
west faster than that, and the
sun never catches you.

69
00:04:30,523 --> 00:04:37,062
It did not buy him more time at home. It
bought him the whole night everywhere else.

70
00:04:37,862 --> 00:04:40,554
Over New York, it was still yesterday.

71
00:04:42,954 --> 00:04:46,415
JONAH: They're under me. The
northern lights are UNDER me!

72
00:04:46,765 --> 00:04:53,211
EXECUTOR: Over northern Canada, the aurora is not
a curtain in the sky. From above, it is a

73
00:04:53,211 --> 00:04:53,688
river.

74
00:04:55,988 --> 00:04:57,912
JONAH: How far is the Moon?

75
00:04:58,262 --> 00:05:00,569
EXECUTOR: Three hundred and
eighty-four thousand kilometres.

76
00:05:00,919 --> 00:05:01,819
JONAH: How long?

77
00:05:02,169 --> 00:05:06,015
EXECUTOR: For this ship? Forty minutes.
Thirty-nine, if you stop asking.

78
00:05:06,815 --> 00:05:11,046
Jonah Okafor, seventeen, of Lagos.
Who had never once left Lagos.

79
00:05:11,396 --> 00:05:12,935
Landed on the Moon.

80
00:05:15,335 --> 00:05:21,815
The ship wrapped him in a bubble of air. Do
not ask me how. I am not permitted to

81
00:05:21,815 --> 00:05:25,335
explain physics you have
not discovered yet.

82
00:05:26,735 --> 00:05:31,735
From the Moon, Earth does not rise
or set. It just hangs there.

83
00:05:32,085 --> 00:05:36,665
Every person he had ever met —
smaller than his thumb.

84
00:05:38,665 --> 00:05:44,761
He found the Apollo 11 landing site. He was
very, very careful not to step on the

85
00:05:44,761 --> 00:05:45,588
footprints.

86
00:05:47,388 --> 00:05:52,773
And on the way home, the ship did
something it had never done before.

87
00:05:53,123 --> 00:05:58,892
A second seat unfolded from the wall. Small.
Far too small for any grown human.

88
00:06:00,492 --> 00:06:02,765
JONAH: Executor... who's this one for?

89
00:06:04,315 --> 00:06:08,546
EXECUTOR: I did not answer. I am
not allowed to. Not yet.

90
00:06:10,346 --> 00:06:15,346
By the third day, everyone knew. Lagos
traffic is famous. It got worse.

91
00:06:15,696 --> 00:06:20,983
NEWS ANCHOR: ...the so-called Heir Number One, a
seventeen-year-old phone repairer from Lagos,

92
00:06:20,983 --> 00:06:22,550
has not been seen since—

93
00:06:23,350 --> 00:06:29,119
GRANDMA: Jonah. There is a man outside in a
suit that costs more than this street.

94
00:06:30,519 --> 00:06:33,212
EXECUTOR: Desmond Kade. The
richest man on Earth.

95
00:06:33,562 --> 00:06:39,619
Until about a week ago, he had assumed that
if anyone was going to inherit the

96
00:06:39,619 --> 00:06:41,638
universe, it would be him.

97
00:06:42,438 --> 00:06:47,438
KADE: I'm not here to take your ship,
Jonah. I'm here to congratulate you.

98
00:06:47,788 --> 00:06:51,250
And to let you know I've filed a contest.

99
00:06:51,600 --> 00:06:52,500
JONAH: A what?

100
00:06:53,300 --> 00:06:58,452
EXECUTOR: Under the will, anyone may contest
an heir. If an heir breaks a rule, the

101
00:06:58,452 --> 00:07:00,992
inheritance passes to the contester.

102
00:07:01,792 --> 00:07:06,023
KADE: Twelve heirs, Jonah. I only
need one of you to slip.

103
00:07:07,823 --> 00:07:14,292
CAPTAIN (RADIO): Mayday, mayday! Fishing boat Ayoola,
taking water — eight crew — we cannot hold her!

104
00:07:15,492 --> 00:07:21,081
EXECUTOR: At 5:40 that morning, a distress call
came in. A boat sinking in a storm, four

105
00:07:21,081 --> 00:07:22,800
hundred kilometres west.

106
00:07:23,150 --> 00:07:24,688
Sunrise in sixty-two minutes.

107
00:07:25,488 --> 00:07:27,796
JONAH: How fast can we get there?

108
00:07:28,146 --> 00:07:30,419
EXECUTOR: Six minutes. And Rule Three—

109
00:07:30,769 --> 00:07:32,308
JONAH: I know Rule Three.

110
00:07:33,108 --> 00:07:35,800
EXECUTOR: The ship could
not carry eight men.

111
00:07:36,150 --> 00:07:38,073
So it carried the boat.

112
00:07:41,473 --> 00:07:47,212
Forty tonnes of wood, nets and terrified
fishermen, lifted out of the Atlantic like

113
00:07:47,212 --> 00:07:47,627
a toy.

114
00:07:49,427 --> 00:07:54,042
By the time the crew stood on
dry sand, it was 6:31.

115
00:07:54,392 --> 00:08:00,546
Lifting the boat had drained the ship. It
could still fly. It could not fly fast.

116
00:08:01,746 --> 00:08:07,359
Home was four hundred kilometres away. The sun
would rise over his street in eleven

117
00:08:07,359 --> 00:08:07,900
minutes.

118
00:08:08,250 --> 00:08:10,942
He was not going to make it.

119
00:08:12,942 --> 00:08:15,250
ASSISTANT: Sir. He won't make it home.

120
00:08:15,600 --> 00:08:16,754
KADE: No. He won't.

121
00:08:18,354 --> 00:08:20,662
JONAH: Executor. Say the
rule again. Exactly.

122
00:08:21,012 --> 00:08:23,704
EXECUTOR: The ship must be
home before sunrise.

123
00:08:24,054 --> 00:08:25,558
JONAH: And "home" means...

124
00:08:25,908 --> 00:08:28,181
EXECUTOR: ...The place where you sleep.

125
00:08:29,781 --> 00:08:34,012
Falling asleep on command is not
a skill most humans have.

126
00:08:34,362 --> 00:08:39,362
Jonah Okafor, who had spent seventeen years
sleeping through Lagos traffic, had it.

127
00:08:40,562 --> 00:08:42,450
FISHERMAN: ...Is he sleeping? Now?

128
00:08:42,800 --> 00:08:49,262
EXECUTOR: At 6:41, on a beach in Ghana, the place
where Jonah slept became home. One minute to

129
00:08:49,262 --> 00:08:49,723
spare.

130
00:08:51,923 --> 00:08:53,812
ASSISTANT: Sir... is that allowed?

131
00:08:54,162 --> 00:08:55,315
KADE: Apparently, it's legal.

132
00:08:56,265 --> 00:08:59,342
Eleven more. Let's see how
clever they are.

133
00:09:00,942 --> 00:09:03,635
EXECUTOR: The next night,
Jonah took a passenger.

134
00:09:03,985 --> 00:09:10,104
GRANDMA: Eighty-one years I have lived in this
city. Nobody told me it was this... shiny.

135
00:09:10,454 --> 00:09:11,608
JONAH: Hold on, Grandma.

136
00:09:11,958 --> 00:09:14,265
GRANDMA: I am holding! I am holding!

137
00:09:16,665 --> 00:09:19,742
JONAH: Executor. The small
seat. Who is it for?

138
00:09:20,092 --> 00:09:23,938
EXECUTOR: Item Thirteen is sealed until
all twelve heirs are together.

139
00:09:24,288 --> 00:09:25,827
JONAH: That's not an answer.

140
00:09:26,177 --> 00:09:27,715
EXECUTOR: No. It's a rule.

141
00:09:28,515 --> 00:09:34,230
Somewhere across the city, an old radio was
playing. It has not missed a night

142
00:09:34,230 --> 00:09:34,669
since.

143
00:09:37,069 --> 00:09:40,146
Heirs found: one of twelve.
Item Thirteen: sealed.

144
00:09:41,746 --> 00:09:42,646
Item Two.

145
00:09:43,296 --> 00:09:46,723
To the one who never wasted a penny...

146
00:09:47,373 --> 00:09:48,912
we leave our asteroid.

147
00:09:50,312 --> 00:09:54,123
And if you're wondering
whether it could be you...

148
00:09:55,073 --> 00:09:56,227
I'm still reading.
